NAME
    trust - approve a module file by SHA-256 hash

SYNOPSIS
    trust <path>

DESCRIPTION
    Computes the SHA-256 digest of <path> (resolved inside the shell
    sandbox) and appends '<sha256>  <resolved-path>' to
    /etc/EmuSen/dianash/trusted. If the file changes later, its hash no
    longer matches and it must be approved again.

    Because approving a module grants it full process privileges, trust
    is permitted only when typed interactively at the prompt; it is
    refused inside source(1) scripts and $(...) command substitutions.

EXAMPLES
    trust /Cores/mymodule.so

EXIT STATUS
    0   File hash recorded in /etc/EmuSen/dianash/trusted.
    1   Missing path, invoked non-interactively, path outside sandbox,
        file missing, or I/O error.

SEE ALSO
    modules(7), cores(1), source(1), hier(7)
